The test `test_body_frag_len_chunked_te` fails because the `ctx.offset` (accumulated body length) does not match the expected `CHUNKED_BODY_SIZE` (16 bytes). This indicates that the `http_client` module, when processing a chunked HTTP response, is including the trailing `\r\n` of a chunk in the reported body fragment length.

The `http_parser` library's `on_body` callback is expected to provide only the decoded body data, stripping any chunk framing. However, in some scenarios or versions, it might include the trailing `\r\n` of a chunk. The `http_client` module's internal `http_client_on_body` callback directly passes the `length` received from `http_parser` to the user's `response_cb` via `rsp->body_frag_len`.

To fix this, the `http_client_on_body` function needs to check if `Transfer-Encoding: chunked` was used and, if so, adjust the `body_frag_len` by removing the trailing `\r\n` if it's present. This ensures that the `response_cb` receives the correct decoded body length.

The fix is applied to `net/lib/http/client.c`, which is part of the Zephyr RTOS HTTP client library.

